      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-1$ and $y\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(x+1)&=(1-y)(1+y)\\\\x^2-1&=1-y^2\\\\x^2+y^2&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe circle has centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\sqrt{2}$.\n\nOn this circle, $x=-1$ gives $y=\\pm1$, and $y=-1$ gives $x=\\pm1$. Exclude $(-1,1)$, $(-1,-1)$ and $(1,-1)$, showing all three as open points.",
